          </p>

          <p>
            Momentous is the priciest at about $3.50 per 25 g, with Truvani close behind. You are paying for NSF Certified for Sport testing, a flavored isolate and a brand that answers the rennet question in writing. That is a fair trade for some buyers, and an unnecessary one for others. If cost matters more than a named enzyme statement, Naked Whey or Naked Casein give you similar protein quality at about half the price.
          </p>

          <p>
            Leucine changes the math slightly. Because soy carries less leucine than whey, you would take roughly 30 g of soy protein to match 25 g of whey, which moves NOW Sports Soy to about $1.24 per whey-equivalent dose. It is still the cheapest option by a wide margin. For more low-cost options across every protein type, see our <a href="/best-cheap-protein-powder/">best cheap protein powder</a> guide.
